
CollidingPixels Level Generator — Version 1  Written by chatGPT - 11/6/2026
For use in generating/validating setup parameters for the PixelPanel game "CollidingPixels".
Once you generate valid round_.a/round_.b/round_.collisionTimeMs values, paste them into CollidingPixelScene.cpp 
in the setupRound() method (adding another case section) and update the CollidingPixelScene.h variable
static constexpr int FINAL_ROUND to match the number of cases in your switch statement.

/* For computing the trajectory of a pixel that bounces off the wall(s)
    We are using a technique known as the method-of-images or unfolding.
    The mirror numbering works like this:
    - 0: The real panel (no reflection).
    - 1: The mirrored panel immediately to the right or above.
    - -1: The mirrored panel immediately to the left or below.
    - 2, -2, etc.: Additional mirrored panels (i.e. more wall bounces).
*/

To run it on your Mac, save the file and execute:
python3 colliding_pixels_generator.py \
    --a 7 2 \
    --b 2 10 \
    --mirror-a 1 0 \
    --mirror-b 0 0 \
    --time 3000 \
    --check 15 20


The --check option validates one specified collision point. Without it, the script searches all 900 possible integer endpoints.
